@startuml component
title payment-platform - modules and how a contract travels

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "payment-platform monorepo" {
  component "person-service" as PS
  component "individuals-api" as API

  artifact "person-service.yaml" as PSY
  artifact "individuals-api.yaml" as IAY
  artifact "V001..V005\nFlyway migrations" as MIG
}

database "Nexus" as NEXUS
artifact "com.dezxxx:person-service-client:1.0.0-SNAPSHOT" as PCJ

PS *-- PSY
PS *-- MIG
API *-- IAY

PSY --> PS : openApiGenerate\nUsersApi server interface\nopenApiGenerateClient\nDTOs + @HttpExchange UsersApi
IAY --> API : openApiGenerate\nAuthApi interface only
PS --> PCJ : make publish\n(the client jar only)
PCJ --> NEXUS
NEXUS --> API : resolved by Maven coordinates\ninside the image build

note bottom of API
  Never project(":person-service").
  Cross-module contracts travel as
  published artifacts, so any module
  can move to its own repository
  without a rewrite.
end note

note right of PS
  One contract, two generations: the server
  interface stays inside person-service, the
  client goes into its own source set and its
  own jar - person-service.jar never carries it.
end note

@enduml
